  "details": "An accessibility issue. People can get medically sick from motion effects. The goal is to make sure users are not harmed or distracted by motion.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Switch into an avatar with a long parameter name or state name.\n\n2. Enable \"Reduce Menu Animations\" in settings.\n\n3. Open the debug UI from the Quick Menu or by pressing RShift + ½ (~) + 2 twice.\n\n4. Switch to Local Avatar. Observe if the long labels are scrolling.\n\nExpected result: No scrolling when this setting is enabled. Alternatively a UI redesign where the labels are shown on cursor hover on a tooltip, or with wider margins for long labels.\n\nActual result: The labels are scrolling with Reduce Menu Animations enabled.\n\nAvatar used in the attached video: `avtr_8a33bffc-c9dd-45a5-a18e-55a18a31c0ef` (private)",
